{"id": "EUVD-2026-92022", "enisaUuid": "9e120f94-583c-3f2a-8604-875ac387b2e5", "description": "OpenAM before 16.1.3 contains an open redirect vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to redirect users by supplying an unverified id_token_hint to the /oauth2/connect/endSession endpoint. Attackers can name any realm client in a forged hint to redirect victims to any registered post-logout URI, enabling phishing that borrows the OpenAM host's trust.", "datePublished": "2026-10-03T12:14:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T14:45:14", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/OpenIdentityPlatform/OpenAM/security/advisories/GHSA-6f8c-crwq-jqm3", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openam-before-16.1.3-open-redirect-via-unverified-id-token-hint-in-endsession"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-105118", "GHSA-mxvw-rw3m-5c33"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c651063b-1c24-3d58-9452-aa008bc47c50", "product": {"name": "OpenAM", "vendor": {"name": "OpenIdentityPlatform"}}, "product_version": "0 <16.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c5daa635-d904-393f-92b0-0fcf3ce6921b", "vendor": {"name": "OpenIdentityPlatform"}}], "isExploited": false}